  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday into Saturday: An upper low will begin to merge with a \nwestern Canada trough today. This will pull up Pacific moisture \nthrough the Desert SW while a surface low developing over southern\nMT and pulls NE, tracking showers across the western and northern \nCWA through Saturday morning. This will also allow NW winds to \nincrease late today behind a cold front. The showers are expected\nto exit the CWA Saturday morning with significantly cooler high \ntemps Saturday onward.\n\nRough conditions on Fort Peck Lake can be expected beginning\nthis afternoon through Saturday afternoon. A Lake wind advisory \nhas been issued for these times. \n\nRainfall amounts looked to be greatest over central Montana and\nthe models have held steady since the last forecast run. Areas \neast of a line from Culbertson to Miles City are not expecting \nany QPF.\n\nSaturday into Tuesday: Temps look to remain below to near normal \nas an upper ridge early next week moves east of the Pac NW.\n\nTuesday night onward: A trough swings through the Pac NW and\nbecome the focal point for newly developing showers mid week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNO changes to NBM.\n\nHigh confidence on winds and temperatures this weekend. \nModerate confidence on rain amounts through those periods. \n\nLow confidence Tuesday onward where ensembles consensus breaks \ndown. Expect many forecast changes from here onward. \n\n/GAH",
